    "compiled_date": "2026-07-29",
    "notes": "El Niño events (positive ENSO anomaly) generally suppress Alaska salmon production by warming the Gulf of Alaska and reducing productivity. La Niña events (negative ENSO) tend to favor Alaska salmon. The NPGO is correlated with nutrient concentrations in the Northeast Pacific — high NPGO = more nutrients = more salmon prey. These indices are used in preseason salmon run forecasting."
  },
